13
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:29,970
In terms of reading
file content,

14
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:32,265
once you've got that file
descriptor from open,

15
00:00:32,265 --> 00:00:33,765
you can use it with read,

16
00:00:33,765 --> 00:00:36,480
very similar to the way
you'd use the filehandle

17
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:39,750
that you use with F read
and buffered IO today.

18
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:42,170
The return value from read
is going to be the number of

19
00:00:42,170 --> 00:00:44,880
bytes read or minus
one on error.

20
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:45,965
If there is an error,

21
00:00:45,965 --> 00:00:49,145
it's going to set errono and
this relates to the Linux,

22
00:00:49,145 --> 00:00:51,635
the discussion that
we talked about in

23
00:00:51,635 --> 00:00:55,295
previous weeks' videos
